; Newsdesk burned-in subtitle style (MOO-425)
;
; Anton, uppercase, ink on a pasteboard halo. Same face as the app's stamps, on
; purpose: the UI spec's continuity rule is that the tool and the media it
; produces should be visibly the same product, and Anton is the one typeface
; both share.
;
; Dark-on-light rather than the usual white-on-black. The house ground is warm
; cream paper (brand-kit/style-tokens.txt), so white captions would dissolve
; into it. Ink fill inside a thick pasteboard outline reads as a printed
; caption pasted onto the collage instead of a broadcast overlay.
;
; Colours are the app's own tokens, not invented ones:
;   ink        #1A1917  ->  &H0017191A
;   pasteboard #E8E6DF  ->  &H00DFE6E8
;   canary     #F2C744  ->  &H0044C7F2   (the UI spec assigns canary to highlights)
; ASS stores colour as &HAABBGGRR — bytes reversed from hex RGB, alpha 00 = opaque.
;
; PlayRes is the 9:16 delivery frame. libass scales outline and shadow with it
; (ScaledBorderAndShadow: yes), so burning at a different output size keeps the
; same proportions rather than producing hairline outlines.
;
; PREREQUISITE FOR ASSEMBLY (Day 4): Anton must be resolvable by libass on the
; machine running the burn. ffmpeg does not embed it — a missing face falls back
; silently to something else, and nobody notices until the render is watched.
; Verify with:  fc-list | grep -i anton

